\ The two scimark kernels whose benchmarks run on zero data: bench/pyperformance/
\ scimark-sor.telic allocates G zero per iteration and scimark-sparse.telic leaves val
\ and x zero, both as pyperformance's bench_SOR and bench_SparseMatMult do, so
\ neither benchmark's checksum can catch wrong arithmetic. These run the same two
\ kernels on seeded data at small sizes, pinning the indexed reads and writes, the
\ float fusions in the stencil and the matvec, and the row/col structure.
\
\ Seeding is a deterministic formula rather than scimark's Random, since what is
\ under test is the kernel arithmetic: cell idx starts at (idx² mod 97) / 97. The
\ formula must be non-linear -- any f linear in idx is an exact fixed point of the
\ stencil (the four neighbours sum to 4·f(idx)), so a linear seed leaves G
\ unchanged and the test proves nothing.

\ === SOR stencil: one 8x8 sweep, interior cells only ===
8.0 constant sor-n
7.0 constant sor-nm1
64.0 constant sor-nn
1.25 0.25 f* constant omega-over-four
1.0 1.25 f- constant one-minus-omega
variable g

: seed-g ^g |
  sor-nn 1 0-matrix to g
  [: i | g  i i f* 97.0 fmod 97.0 f/  i  !e drop :] sor-nn i-times ;

: sor-sweep ( cycles -- )
  | cycles |
  0.0 to cycle
  begin cycle cycles < while
     1.0 to y
     begin y sor-nm1 < while
        y sor-n f* to rowbase
        1.0 to x
        begin x sor-nm1 < while
           rowbase x f+ to idx
           g idx sor-n f- @e
           g idx sor-n f+ @e f+
           g idx 1.0 f- @e f+
           g idx 1.0 f+ @e f+
           omega-over-four f*
           one-minus-omega  g idx @e f*  f+  to nv
           g nv idx !e drop
           f++ x
        repeat
        f++ y
     repeat
     f++ cycle
  repeat ;

: g-checksum ( -- s )  0.0 [: g swap @e f+ :] sor-nn i-times ;

seed-g
g-checksum . cr                        \ 32.8351
1.0 sor-sweep
g-checksum . cr                        \ 31.789
g 9 @e . cr                            \ 0.316366
g 54 @e . cr                           \ 0.503945
3.0 sor-sweep
g-checksum . cr                        \ 31.1138

clear

\ === compressed-row sparse matvec: N=16, 4 nonzeros per row, 3 cycles ===
16.0 constant sp-n
4.0 constant sp-nr
64.0 constant sp-anz
variable row  variable col  variable val  variable x  variable y

: seed-sparse ^row ^col ^val ^x ^y |
  sp-n 1.0 f+ 1 0-matrix to row
  sp-anz 1 0-matrix to col
  sp-anz 1 0-matrix to val
  sp-n 1 0-matrix to x
  sp-n 1 0-matrix to y
  [: i | x  i 1.0 f+ sp-n f/  i  !e drop :] sp-n i-times
  [: i | val  i 2.0 f* 1.0 f+ sp-anz f/  i  !e drop :] sp-anz i-times
  row 0.0 0.0 !e drop
  [: | r |
     row r @e to rowr
     row  rowr sp-nr f+  r 1.0 f+  !e drop
     r sp-nr / ftruncate to step
     step 1.0 < if 1.0 to step then
     rowr step
     [: dup 2 pick f*  swap 3 pick f+  col -rot  !e drop :] sp-nr i-times
     drop drop
  :] sp-n i-times ;

: matvec ( cycles -- )
  [:
     [: | r |
        row r @e to lo
        row r 1.0 f+ @e to hi
        lo 0.0
        [: | k | 1 pick k f+ to i  x col i @e @e  val i @e f*  f+ :] hi lo f- i-times
        nip
        y swap r !e drop
     :] sp-n i-times
  :] swap times ;

: y-checksum ( -- s )  0.0 [: y swap @e f+ :] sp-n i-times ;

seed-sparse
3.0 matvec
y-checksum . cr                        \ 17.3984
y 0 @e . cr                            \ 0.0488281
y 15 @e . cr                           \ 2.69336
row 16 @e . cr                         \ 64
col 63 @e . cr                         \ 9

bye
